# Nanotrasen Representative SOP

[bold]1.[/bold] The NanoTrasen Representative is to ensure that every Department is following Standard Operating Procedure, up to and including the respective [color=#8ec8ff]Head of Staff[/color]. If a [color=#8ec8ff]Head of Staff[/color] is not available for a Department, the NanoTrasen Representative must ensure that the [color=#8ec8ff]Captain[/color] appoints an [color=#8ec8ff]Acting Head of Staff[/color] for said Department if a suitable and willing candidate can be found;

[bold]2.[/bold] The NanoTrasen Representative must attempt to resolve any breach of Standard Operating Procedure locally before contacting [color=#7dffa8]Central Command[/color].

[bold]3.[/bold] In the absense of a [color=#ff8a8a]Magistrate[/color], the NanoTrasen Representative must ensure that space law is being adequately followed and enforced.

[bold]4.[/bold] The NanoTrasen Representative may administer class 1 and 2 penalties for misconduct concerning Standard Operating Procedure. They may only administer penalties for misconduct concerning misinterpretation of [textlink="Space Law" link="SpaceLaw"] in the absense of a [color=#ff8a8a]Magistrate[/color], and may never administer class 3 penalties even when there is no [color=#ff8a8a]Magistrate[/color];

[bold]5.[/bold] The NanoTrasen Representative must follow the directions of the [color=#ff8a8a]Magistrate[/color] and defer to their judgement in matters not concerning standard operating procedure, but should advocate their stance firmly in the case of disagreements, and escalate to [color=#7dffa8]Central Command[/color] directly if they feel there has been wrongdoing;

[bold]6.[/bold] The NanoTrasen Representative is permitted to carry their flash, a blade-cane, and a standard-issue sidearm (i.e., MK-58 or RG-2);

## Nanotrasen Representative OOC Rules and Expectations
The purpose and spirit of the NTR is to be the stations foremost expert and authority regarding the minutia of Standard Operating Procedure. They create meaningful role play by keeping the IAA's overzealous punitive measures in check, acting as an authority to which crew can complain about the IAA's, and performing regular, less zealous inspections of departments.
